WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.969 --> 00:00:05.189
One of the most difficult skills to improve
through real-life situations is listening.

00:00:05.189 --> 00:00:10.310
But have no fear – you can target your learning
to make it a breeze!

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.000
Here are four ways to make this happen.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:19.099
If you know you're going into a situation
where English is spoken, you can prepare yourself

00:00:19.099 --> 00:00:23.119
by brushing up on the likely words which could
be used.

00:00:23.119 --> 00:00:27.069
For example, if you're going to the airport,
you're most likely to hear things about your

00:00:27.069 --> 00:00:30.839
flight, destination, visa and luggage.

00:00:30.839 --> 00:00:35.140
Before you go to the airport, you can review
the vocabulary related to these topics.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:39.870
Don’t forget, if you don’t catch everything
the first time, it's okay to ask them to repeat

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.000
it for you, which is also good practice.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:47.820
You can also practise by listening for specific
information.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:53.320
If we go back to the airport example, you
could listen out for your destination or flight

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:54.550
number.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:57.200
This will keep the learning focused and practical
for you.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:03.350
Like with reading, you can choose what you
want to listen to for practice.

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:07.820
If you're a TV or film fan, try watching a
section without subtitles and then watch again

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:10.000
with subtitles to check your understanding.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:15.630
You can also listen to radio programmes or
podcasts from all over the world.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:19.240
Choose a topic you're interested in and you’ll
be amazed how many interesting programmes

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:20.000
are available!

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:26.790
It may be hard to believe, but watching people
can also help you listen.

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:28.470
How does this work?

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:32.940
When people talk, they normally use more than
just their words to communicate.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:36.900
They're conveying meaning with their tone
of voice, hand gestures, the way they sit

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.960
or stand, and so on.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.910
Carefully observe the people you listen to.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:45.000
Linking it all together can help make the
meaning clear to you.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:50.420
One thing to be aware of here is that there
may be cultural differences in body language.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:54.201
If you are visiting somewhere new, it’s
a good idea to have a quick read about the

00:01:54.201 --> 00:01:55.969
customs and culture of the place beforehand.

